  "id": "COMPOUND:27344 - PROTEIN:5011",
  "verbalization": "The visible evidence suggests a potential relationship between 7-Deacetyl-7-benzoylepoxyazadiradione and HCC1937 through a series of target interactions involving thioredoxin, mitochondrial, and other compounds. The drug is implicated in targeting thioredoxin, a protein involved in cellular redox regulation, and this target is in turn linked to interiorin and isotorachrysone-6-O-alpha-D-ribofuranoside, which both ultimately target HCC1937. These pathways highlight a complex network of molecular interactions, where the drug may influence cellular processes through the modulation of thioredoxin, potentially leading to effects on HCC1937. The integration of these targets suggests a possible mechanism by which the drug exerts its influence, though the exact nature of the interaction remains to be fully elucidated.",
